┌── Log ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           Some went home. Some are still on the roads, in their old companies, under their old   │
│           captains.                                                                              │
│                                                                                                  │
│           In the Thornmarch, at the far edge of the kingdom, an exile chops wood.                │
│                                                                                                  │
│           Hollis sits on the block by the fire with one of Ellery's boots on his knee and an     │
│           awl in his fist. He has not slept. There is a folded paper in his coat that he keeps   │
│           touching.                                                                              │
│                                                                                                  │
│           Hollis Marr                                                                            │
│           Sideways, with the grain. You'll have the axe in your foot, and then who mends the     │
│           boot? Give me the other one.                                                           │
│                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│ ▶         Hollis Marr                                                                            │
│           Forty years on my feet in other people's boots. Never seen the sea. Did you know       │
│           that? Forty years. Pass me the thread.                                                 │
│                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│           Ellery                                                                                 │
│           Why the sea?                                                                           │
│                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│           Hollis Marr                                                                            │
│           Because it's the one thing the boy wrote home about from the war that I believed.      │
│           ...There. Try that. And what'll you do, when this lifts? It lifts. Kings forget.       │
│                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│           Back to latest                                                                         │
